"I6sZKT5Dt","title":"The Morning Brew","url":"https://blog.cwa.me.uk/2024/02/21/the-morning-brew-3886/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/the-morning-brew-i6szkt5dt","summary":"This post covers topics such as installing extensions without restarting Visual Studio, configuration-as-code customization in Microsoft Dev Box, and mapping SQL results to any object using Entity Framework Core 8.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/f05a15313e5701cfbe1bf5bad3c124fd?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":2,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-02-21T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"gsg0aFJlD","title":"GitHub Quick Reviews","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4y8z17ev3Wk","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/github-quick-reviews-gsg0afjld","summary":null,"image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/4y8z17ev3Wk/sddefault_live.jpg","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-02-20T18:03:17.000Z"},{"id":"Hi1yyUT0F","title":"Using Azure Key Vault for signing and encrypting JSON Web Tokens","url":"https://joonasw.net/view/using-azure-key-vault-for-signing-and-encrypting-json-web-tokens","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/using-azure-key-vault-for-signing-and-encrypting-json-web-tokens-hi1yyut0f","summary":"This post explores how to sign and encrypt JSON Web Tokens (JWTs) using Azure Key Vault keys and certificates. It also discusses key rotation and performance optimizations for cryptographic operations.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/12d9a370cc41c14496bc98fa267e9d67?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":3,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-02-20T14:50:52.000Z"},{"id":"WBnpdoeBh","title":"How to Set up Netlify Deploys for Docfx using GitHub Actions","url":"https://seankilleen.com/2024/02/how-to-set-up-netlify-deploys-for-docfx-using-github-actions/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/how-to-set-up-netlify-deploys-for-docfx-using-github-actions-wbnpdoebh","summary":"Learn how to set up Netlify Deploys for Docfx using GitHub Actions and deploy to Netlify for live previews within pull requests.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/e821933ccaf53bd5891661f998aecb42?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":2,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-02-20T12:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"ZwPvz4EhJ","title":"Book Review: Angular Cookbook","url":"https://codingsonata.com/book-review-angular-cookbook/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/book-review-angular-cookbook-zwpvz4ehj","summary":"Angular Cookbook is a comprehensive book that covers various topics in Angular, including component communication, directives, dependency injection, animations, RxJS, state management, routing, forms, testing, PWA, and more. The book is recommended for mid-level Angular developers who want to deepen their understanding of Angular concepts and build enterprise-grade applications.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":5,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-02-20T07:47:00.000Z"},{"id":"5DK4tZ41M","title":"Avoid multiple boolean parameters","url":"https://steven-giesel.com/blogPost/9994b00c-8bc2-4794-ae74-80e6ee4cd5e5","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/avoid-multiple-boolean-parameters-5dk4tz41m","summary":"Learn why multiple boolean parameters can make code more difficult to reason about and how to refactor them for clearer code.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/0e7c25469755582074c192b295d3a63d?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":2,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-02-20T04:35:00.000Z"}],"top_posts":[{"id":"MmcWTdCza","title":"#React Is WORSE Than #Angular!","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YBIZfDItL3E","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/react-is-worse-than-angular--mmcwtdcza","summary":"Next.js is more opinionated than Angular, which is surprising considering React's reputation for being flexible and non-opinionated.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/YBIZfDItL3E/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":13,"num_comments":8,"created_at":"2024-01-25T17:17:14.000Z"},{"id":"8ANdR7Zf2","title":"What Is A JavaScript Bundler?","url":"https://www.codejourney.net/what-is-a-javascript-bundler/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/what-is-a-javascript-bundler--8andr7zf2","summary":"A JavaScript bundler produces bundles. It's basically a static file, optimized to be served to the client (in our case: a web browser) The main goal is to produce a single bundle file from multiple dependencies. In effect, the user\u2019s browser doesn\u2019t need to fetch so many files separately.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/fba032861f74b2c4fca649190e958466?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":42,"num_comments":1,"created_at":"2023-09-02T08:16:11.000Z"},{"id":"UpmnPjkrX","title":"\"Clean Architecture\" and indirection. No thanks.","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_rgH0Kb9Bis","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/clean-architecture-and-indirection-no-thanks--upmnpjkrx","summary":null,"image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/_rgH0Kb9Bis/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":45,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-06-15T12:28:12.000Z"},{"id":"zfG17Fqoh","title":"How (And Why?) To Wrap External Libraries?","url":"https://www.codejourney.net/how-and-why-to-wrap-external-libraries/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/how-and-why-to-wrap-external-libraries--zfg17fqoh","summary":"Learn how and why to wrap external libraries to make your life easier and abstract your code from their implementation details.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/c8d14fd09802d623203903066e7fc40d?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":30,"num_comments":3,"created_at":"2023-02-20T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"lUXL8WGCs","title":"Using your Database as a Queue?","url":"https://codeopinion.com/using-your-database-as-a-queue/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/using-your-database-as-a-queue--luxl8wgcs","